FSPEED-CTR-TRACE lane=gbdt-categorical MOJOLEARN_CTR_TRACE=1 (the fit prints its CTR config split and prep marker; DEVIATION 2634 is observable)
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=1.000000 reason=categorical method: ours follows CatBoost's dispatch (one-hot at or below one_hot_max_size, CTR target statistics above), CatBoost runs its own at its defaults: two libraries, one algorithm, on the same declared columns
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=2.000000 reason=categorical method: XGBoost partition search (enable_categorical, max_cat_to_onehot 1), LightGBM its own categorical split (categorical_feature) at its defaults (max_cat_to_onehot, cat_smooth, cat_l2): different algorithms from CTR
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=3.000000 reason=input conversion inside the fit clock: CatBoost gets the declared columns as int64 (it refuses float categorical columns), XGBoost a pandas frame with one CategoricalDtype per column; ours and LightGBM take the float32 codes
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=4.000000 reason=LightGBM min_child_samples 20 and min_child_weight 1e-3 stay at its defaults: at 0 (the gbdt lanes' value) LightGBM 4.7.0 aborts the first categorical tree
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=mismatch delta=5.000000 reason=codes are dense 0..k-1 within the train slice (our fit refuses a non-dense categorical column); a test value unseen in training shares one unknown bucket k per column
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=* metric=objectives delta=4.000000 reason=catboost Logloss; lightgbm binary; mojolearn Logloss; xgboost binary:logistic
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=ours metric=devices delta=1.000000 reason=devices=cpu (explicit); on an NVIDIA box the vendors' CPU arms do not run, so a lane whose only opponent is a CPU library has NO legal opponent here and says so
BENCH_BINDING arm=ours requested=identical resolved=identical compiled=identical vendor=metal path=/Users/ec2-user/bench-board-cache/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/mojolearn/identical/_mojolearn_gbdt.so
BENCH_PATHS arm=ours 2550_borrow_x=1 2551_device_partition=1 2580_level_quant=0 2581_group_width=1
FSPEED-AB lane=gbdt-categorical arm=ours-ab numeric_mode='fast' (arm ours keeps the estimator default)
BENCH_BINDING arm=ours-ab requested=fast resolved=fast compiled=fast vendor=metal path=/Users/ec2-user/bench-board-cache/venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/mojolearn/_mojolearn_gbdt.so
BENCH_PATHS arm=ours-ab 2550_borrow_x=1 2551_device_partition=0 2580_level_quant=0 2581_group_width=0
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=catboost-cpu,ours metric=mismatch delta=1.000000 reason=score_function: ours (and catboost-gpu) NewtonL2, catboost-cpu Cosine: CatBoost's CPU learner scores splits with Cosine or L2 only (leafwise_scoring.cpp); XGBoost and LightGBM have one Newton L2 gain
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-categorical arms=lightgbm-* metric=mismatch delta=2.000000 reason=LightGBM min_data_in_bin 3 (its default; ours, CatBoost and XGBoost have no minimum bin count) and a 200,000-row bin sample (ours border_build_max_samples 200000, CatBoost's 200000, XGBoost sketches every row)
